  "user_handle": "dee24",
  "body": "# CrossAdapter doesn't handle inverse direction in updatePriceFeeds\n\n## Summary\n\nThe CrossAdapter contract supports both forward and inverse direction for price queries (like getQuote), but it forgot to add the same direction logic in updatePriceFeeds. This causes price updates to fail when called in the inverse direction.\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\nCrossAdapter is designed to chain two oracles together. For example, to price wstETH/USD, it goes through stETH as a middle token:\n- Forward: wstETH → stETH → USD\n- Inverse: USD → stETH → wstETH\n\nThe contract has a function called `getQuote` that correctly handles both directions:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _getQuote(uint256 inAmount, address _base, address _quote) internal view override returns (uint256) {\n    bool inverse = ScaleUtils.getDirectionOrRevert(_base, base, _quote, quote); // Checks direction\n    \n    if (inverse) {\n        // Inverse path: calls oracleCrossQuote first, then oracleBaseCross\n        inAmount = IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).getQuote(inAmount, quote, cross);\n        return IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).getQuote(inAmount, cross, base);\n    } else {\n        // Forward path: calls oracleBaseCross first, then oracleCrossQuote\n        inAmount = IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).getQuote(inAmount, base, cross);\n        return IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).getQuote(inAmount, cross, quote);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nBut when we look at `updatePriceFeeds`, it's missing this direction check:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _updatePriceFeeds(address _base, address _quote, bytes calldata updateData) internal override {\n    // NO direction check here! Just always does the same thing\n    \n    uint128 baseFee = IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).getUpdateFee(_base, cross, crossUpdateData[0]);\n    uint128 quoteFee = IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).getUpdateFee(_quote, cross, crossUpdateData[1]);\n    \n    IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).updatePriceFeeds{value: baseFee}(_base, cross, crossUpdateData[0]);\n    IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).updatePriceFeeds{value: quoteFee}(_quote, cross, crossUpdateData[1]);\n}\n```\n\n### What goes wrong\n\nLet's say we have CrossAdapter set up like this:\n- base = wstETH\n- cross = stETH\n- quote = USD\n- oracleBaseCross = handles wstETH/stETH\n- oracleCrossQuote = handles stETH/USD\n\n**Forward direction (BASE, QUOTE) - Works fine:**\n```solidity\nupdatePriceFeeds(wstETH, USD, data)\n→ calls oracleBaseCross with (wstETH, stETH)  Correct\n→ calls oracleCrossQuote with (USD, stETH)  Correct\n```\n\n**Inverse direction (QUOTE, BASE) - Breaks:**\n```solidity\nupdatePriceFeeds(USD, wstETH, data)\n→ calls oracleBaseCross with (USD, stETH)  Wrong! This oracle doesn't handle USD\n→ calls oracleCrossQuote with (wstETH, stETH)  Wrong! This oracle doesn't handle wstETH\n```\n\nThe oracles return wrong fees (likely 0) because they're being asked about token pairs they don't know about. Then the transaction reverts because the total fee doesn't match what was sent.\n\n## Impact\n\n1. **Price updates fail in inverse direction** - Any call to updatePriceFeeds with inverse parameters will revert\n2. **Prices become stale** - If a market needs inverse direction pricing, it can't update prices\n3. **Users get bad rates** - Stale prices mean users trade at worse rates than they should\n4. **Inconsistent behavior** - getQuote works both ways, but updatePriceFeeds only works one way\n\nThis is clearly a bug and not how it's supposed to work because:\n- The contract documentation explicitly mentions \"inverse direction\" \n- There's a test that checks inverse direction for getQuote\n- getQuote and previewGetQuote both handle inverse correctly\n- Only updatePriceFeeds is missing this logic\n\n\nThe test proves:\n1. Inverse direction is supposed to work (it works for getQuote)\n2. Inverse direction fails for updatePriceFeeds (missing direction check)\n\n## Recommended Fix\n\nAdd the same direction check that getQuote uses to updatePriceFeeds:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _updatePriceFeeds(address _base, address _quote, bytes calldata updateData) internal override {\n    if (updateData.length == 0) {\n        if (msg.value > 0) revert Errors.PriceOracle_IncorrectPayment();\n    } else {\n        bytes[] memory crossUpdateData = abi.decode(updateData, (bytes[]));\n        if (crossUpdateData.length != 2) revert Errors.PriceOracle_InvalidUpdateData();\n\n        // ADD THIS: Check which direction we're going\n        bool inverse = ScaleUtils.getDirectionOrRevert(_base, base, _quote, quote);\n\n        uint128 baseFee;\n        uint128 quoteFee;\n\n        if (inverse) {\n            // For inverse direction: quote→cross→base\n            quoteFee = IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).getUpdateFee(_base, cross, crossUpdateData[0]);\n            baseFee = IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).getUpdateFee(cross, _quote, crossUpdateData[1]);\n        } else {\n            // For forward direction: base→cross→quote\n            baseFee = IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).getUpdateFee(_base, cross, crossUpdateData[0]);\n            quoteFee = IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).getUpdateFee(cross, _quote, crossUpdateData[1]);\n        }\n\n        if (msg.value != (baseFee + quoteFee)) revert Errors.PriceOracle_IncorrectPayment();\n\n        if (inverse) {\n            IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).updatePriceFeeds{value: quoteFee}(_base, cross, crossUpdateData[0]);\n            IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).updatePriceFeeds{value: baseFee}(cross, _quote, crossUpdateData[1]);\n        } else {\n            IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).updatePriceFeeds{value: baseFee}(_base, cross, crossUpdateData[0]);\n            IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).updatePriceFeeds{value: quoteFee}(cross, _quote, crossUpdateData[1]);\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nDo the same fix for `_getUpdateFee`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _getUpdateFee(address _base, address _quote, bytes calldata updateData) \n    internal view override returns (uint128) {\n    if (updateData.length == 0) {\n        return 0;\n    } else {\n        bytes[] memory crossUpdateData = abi.decode(updateData, (bytes[]));\n        if (crossUpdateData.length != 2) revert Errors.PriceOracle_InvalidUpdateData();\n\n        // ADD THIS: Check direction\n        bool inverse = ScaleUtils.getDirectionOrRevert(_base, base, _quote, quote);\n\n        uint128 baseFee;\n        uint128 quoteFee;\n\n        if (inverse) {\n            quoteFee = IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).getUpdateFee(_base, cross, crossUpdateData[0]);\n            baseFee = IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).getUpdateFee(cross, _quote, crossUpdateData[1]);\n        } else {\n            baseFee = IPriceOracle(oracleBaseCross).getUpdateFee(_base, cross, crossUpdateData[0]);\n            quoteFee = IPriceOracle(oracleCrossQuote).getUpdateFee(cross, _quote, crossUpdateData[1]);\n        }\n\n        return baseFee + quoteFee;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis makes updatePriceFeeds work the same way as getQuote - checking direction and calling the right oracles in the right order.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\nI created a test that shows the bug.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {StubPriceOracle} from \"../../mocks/StubPriceOracle.sol\";\nimport {CrossAdapter} from \"../../../src/curators/oracles/CrossAdapter.sol\";\nimport {Errors} from \"../../../src/curators/lib/Errors.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title CrossAdapter Inverse Direction Bug - Proof of Concept\n * @notice Demonstrates that CrossAdapter.updatePriceFeeds() fails for inverse direction\n */\ncontract CrossAdapterInverseBugPoC is Test {\n    address BASE = makeAddr(\"BASE\");\n    address CROSS = makeAddr(\"CROSS\");\n    address QUOTE = makeAddr(\"QUOTE\");\n\n    StubPriceOracle oracleBaseCross;\n    StubPriceOracle oracleCrossQuote;\n    CrossAdapter oracle;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        oracleBaseCross = new StubPriceOracle();\n        oracleCrossQuote = new StubPriceOracle();\n        oracle = new CrossAdapter(BASE, CROSS, QUOTE, address(oracleBaseCross), address(oracleCrossQuote));\n    }\n\n    /// @notice BASELINE: getQuote works in FORWARD direction\n    function test_BASELINE_GetQuote_Forward_Works() public {\n        oracleBaseCross.setPrice(BASE, CROSS, 1e18);\n        oracleCrossQuote.setPrice(CROSS, QUOTE, 1e18);\n\n        uint256 result = oracle.getQuote(1000, BASE, QUOTE);\n        assertGt(result, 0);\n    }\n\n    /// @notice BASELINE: getQuote works in INVERSE direction\n    function test_BASELINE_GetQuote_Inverse_Works() public {\n        oracleCrossQuote.setPrice(QUOTE, CROSS, 1e18);\n        oracleBaseCross.setPrice(CROSS, BASE, 1e18);\n\n        uint256 result = oracle.getQuote(1000, QUOTE, BASE);\n        assertGt(result, 0);\n    }\n\n    /// @notice BASELINE: updatePriceFeeds works in FORWARD direction\n    function test_BASELINE_UpdatePriceFeeds_Forward_Works() public {\n        bytes memory baseCrossData = abi.encode(\"baseCrossData\");\n        bytes memory crossQuoteData = abi.encode(\"crossQuoteData\");\n\n        bytes[] memory arr = new bytes[](2);\n        arr[0] = baseCrossData;\n        arr[1] = crossQuoteData;\n        bytes memory updateData = abi.encode(arr);\n\n        oracleBaseCross.setUpdateFee(BASE, CROSS, baseCrossData, 100);\n        oracleCrossQuote.setUpdateFee(QUOTE, CROSS, crossQuoteData, 200);\n\n        oracle.updatePriceFeeds{value: 300}(BASE, QUOTE, updateData);\n    }\n\n    /// @notice  BUG: updatePriceFeeds FAILS in INVERSE direction\n    function test_BUG_UpdatePriceFeeds_Inverse_FAILS() public {\n        bytes memory crossQuoteData = abi.encode(\"crossQuoteData\");\n        bytes memory baseCrossData = abi.encode(\"baseCrossData\");\n\n        bytes[] memory arr = new bytes[](2);\n        arr[0] = crossQuoteData;\n        arr[1] = baseCrossData;\n        bytes memory updateData = abi.encode(arr);\n\n        // Set fees correctly for inverse direction\n        oracleCrossQuote.setUpdateFee(QUOTE, CROSS, crossQuoteData, 100);\n        oracleBaseCross.setUpdateFee(CROSS, BASE, baseCrossData, 200);\n\n        // THE BUG: CrossAdapter calls wrong oracles with wrong parameters\n        // It calls: oracleBaseCross.getUpdateFee(QUOTE, CROSS) - returns 0 (not set)\n        // It calls: oracleCrossQuote.getUpdateFee(BASE, CROSS) - returns 0 (not set)\n        // Total calculated: 0, but we send 300 -> Revert!\n\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.PriceOracle_IncorrectPayment.selector);\n        oracle.updatePriceFeeds{value: 300}(QUOTE, BASE, updateData);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSave File:\n`test/oracles/adapters/Crossadapterinversebugpoc.t.sol`\n\nTo run the test:\n```bash\nforge test --match-contract CrossAdapterInverseBugPoC -vvv\n```",
